xai-grok-markdown and xai-grok-markdown-core retain upstream implementation,
tests, mermaid/table playgrounds, and the tokyo-night/Swift syntax assets.
Cargo.toml files only add `publish = false` and resolve workspace dependencies
in rust/Cargo.toml. Local NOTICE files exist so packed native licenses can copy
an Apache-2.0 notice beside LICENSE. Fuzz targets were not imported.

xai-ratatui-textarea and xai-ratatui-inline retain upstream implementation,
examples and tests. Five textarea test files have mechanical Rust 1.98 lint fixes:
redundant imports/formatting borrows removed and single-Range slices spelled
unambiguously; assertions and runtime semantics are unchanged. Modified files
carry local notices. Their Cargo workspace dependencies resolve in rust/Cargo.toml.
The inline crate is linked for official fullscreen/minimal rendering: fullscreen
uses the alternate-screen lifecycle, and minimal emits committed turns through
`emit_to_scrollback` into native history with an inline overlay. Cargo.lock began
with the pinned export's lockfile and was pruned by Cargo to this workspace's
actual dependencies.

src/welcome/layout.rs is extracted from xai-grok-pager/src/views/welcome/mod.rs.
src/welcome/hero_box.rs is extracted from the sibling hero_box.rs. Local changes
remove remote announcements, auth, session pickers, changelogs, and unused result
fields. The wide/stacked sizing and draft layout algorithms are retained.
src/welcome/logo.rs retains the upstream logo sizing and shimmer machinery with
codsh ASCII art, an offline palette, and removal of unused entry points.
src/welcome/menu.rs retains the menu rendering and selection machinery with
narrow-window clipping and the offline palette. Modified files carry notices.

src/theme.rs now owns the isolated theme catalog, quantization, and
minimal/terminal-native palette contract. src/appearance.rs, src/settings_ui.rs,
and src/status_line.rs are codsh-owned adapters: they persist `/settings` and
`/theme` into `$GROK_HOME/config.toml`, preview without writing, refuse
repository status-line commands, time out status-line scripts, and kill leftover
process groups. They do not import upstream agent, tool, login, or telemetry crates.

The new main, terminal guard, palette, and welcome composition are codsh code.
src/prompt_edit.rs is a host around xai-ratatui-textarea: it keeps that editor's
key classification, undo, paste, and Unicode handling, and adds history search,
slash/HISTFILE completion, multiline chord swap, prompt Vim via
`[ui] simple_mode`, ghost-text acceptance, and $VISUAL/$EDITOR/vi round-trips.
It does not replace the textarea input state machine.
They do not import upstream agent, tool, login, update, telemetry, feedback,
network, or canonical session crates. Prompt submission refuses execution and
preserves the draft; it does not fabricate an answer or a connected runtime.
This ticket does not claim full UI parity, minimal-mode parity, or a dsh turn.

Ticket 11 (#143) adds local `src/filesystem_sandbox.rs`. It uses the Apache-2.0
`nono` 0.53 crate (Seatbelt/Landlock) and does not import `xai-grok-sandbox`.
Network filtering and bubblewrap re-exec are not included.

Ticket 25 (#157) adapts the dropped-path classifier of
xai-grok-pager-render/src/prompt_images.rs (`try_read_dropped_paths` and its
quote/`file://`/backslash-escape helpers) into local `src/dropped_paths.rs`,
which carries a notice. Local changes take only all-image drops (a non-image
path keeps the codsh workspace-file drop), omit the unexpanded `~/` and Windows
drive/UNC anchors and the tracing target, and hand each file to the local
png/jpeg/webp/gif sniffer with its 256 KiB ceiling. A dropped `.png` that is
corrupt, empty, or not one of those types therefore shows a notice and inserts
nothing, where upstream lets it fall through as its path text; one over 256 KiB
gets the same notice, where upstream attaches it up to its own larger limits.

Ticket 57 (#189) adds local `src/auth.rs` and `src/extra_ca.rs` for substitute
login/logout/setup, extra CA trust, and signed managed-config fetch. Those
modules do not import upstream xai-grok-login or official entitlements.

Ticket 49 (#181) vendors the Apache-2.0 `xai-workflow` crate (the reference
Rhai workflow engine, crates/codegen/xai-workflow) as upstream/xai-workflow.
Its sources and example are unchanged except src/engine.rs, which carries a
header note and replaces one `match` with `?` for the current Clippy
(question_mark); behaviour is identical. Cargo.toml adds `publish = false`, and
a NOTICE was added for packed native licenses. The crate's own tests run with
the workspace. The host side is local `src/workflow.rs` (the hidden
`__workflow-engine` JSON-line subcommand, the reference registry's
source-resolution rules, and the reference host's agent-option checks) and
`packages/cli/bin/rust-acp-workflow.mjs`; neither imports the reference
workflow manager, host service, or session crates. The engine's operation and
size limits are not a security sandbox. rhai_codegen 3.2.0 ships no license
file, so its MIT and Apache-2.0 texts come from the rhai repository at the
crate's VCS revision recorded in import.json.

Ticket 50 (#182) adds local `src/workflow_host.rs` with the reference host's
workflow contracts: the output-contract prompt and correction prompt, the
schema compile limits (256 KB, no external `$ref`, bounded regexes) and the
answer parsing order, the scratch-file limits and messages, and the
`git_diff_since` commit check, timeout, and cap. It is written against the
reference host_service.rs and schema_contract.rs behaviour, not copied, and
imports no reference crate. Schema validation adds the MIT `jsonschema` crate
at the reference version (=0.30.0, default features off) with its dependency
closure; `tempfile` becomes a normal dependency for atomic scratch writes.
uuid-simd 0.8.0 and vsimd 0.8.0 (pulled in by jsonschema's format checks) ship
no license file, so their MIT text comes from the Nugine/simd repository at the
crate VCS revision recorded in import.json.

