Ticket 55 (#187) adds local `src/image_gen.rs` and
`packages/cli/bin/rust-acp-image.mjs`, written against the reference
crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/{image_gen,
image_edit}/mod.rs, grok_build/storage.rs, xai-grok-tools-api/src/
slash_commands.rs and the shell's /imagine command at the pinned commit
(Apache-2.0, see LICENSE), not copied. The `/imagine` instruction and usage
text are copied verbatim; the tool schemas keep the reference argument names
and wording, with "xAI Imagine" replaced by "the configured image service".
Local changes to the reference behavior: the service is any configured
substitute (`xai` reference JSON or `openai` Images protocol) and official
hosts are refused instead of calling the Imagine account; there is no tier
upsell; like the reference only `b64_json` is read, and a URL-only reply is
named as such and never fetched; saved files keep the returned format (png/jpg/webp/gif) instead
of always `.jpg`; references are sent as given (up to 20 MiB each) instead of
being re-encoded to 768 px / 400 KiB; every call asks through the dsh
approval path; the editor ACP server offers no image tools.

Ticket 56 (#188) adds local `src/video_gen.rs` and
`packages/cli/bin/rust-acp-video.mjs`, written against the reference
crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/video_gen/mod.rs,
xai-grok-tools/src/media_gen/limits.rs, the pager's slash_commands/
imagine_video.rs and render_video_overlay.rs at the pinned commit (Apache-2.0,
see LICENSE), not copied. The `/imagine-video` instruction and usage text are
copied verbatim; the tool schemas keep the reference argument names and
wording, with the service branding (including the voice list text) replaced by
"the configured video service". Local changes to the reference behavior: the
service is any configured substitute (`xai` reference async API or the
stable-diffusion.cpp `sdcpp` job API) and official hosts are refused instead of
calling the Imagine account; there is no tier upsell, no ZDR/S3 upload path and
no model override; the schema's duration and resolution limits come from the
configured service's declared capabilities and anything outside them is
refused before a request instead of being defaulted; a finished xai video is
downloaded only from `base_url`'s host or `video_download_hosts`; every job is
recorded in `<session>/video-jobs/` so timeout, cancel (with the service's
answer), an interrupted runner and a later `/videos status` query are
distinguishable; videos are saved as `<session>/videos/<n>.<ext>` in the
returned container; every call asks through the dsh approval path; the editor
ACP server offers no video tools.

upstream/import.json records original source paths and SHA-256 digests.
scripts/build-rust.mjs records the native artifact's normal/build dependency
closure and carries dependency license/notice files into npm packing, refusing
missing license texts. Supplemental texts for ratatui-core/tui-scrollbar come
from the crates.io VCS revisions recorded in import.json.
No binary is committed or automatically published.

